Title:          docker.tcz
Description:    TESTING Docker Engine static binaries for CorePure64
Version:        29.10.0
Author:         Docker, Inc. and Moby contributors
Original-site:  https://www.docker.com/
Copying-policy: Apache-2.0
Size:           85M
Extension_by:   homecore
Tags:           docker containers engine corepure64
Comments:       binary-only
                ----------
                Packages Docker Engine static binaries (cli, dockerd,
                containerd, runc, docker-proxy, docker-init) for
                Tiny Core Linux CorePure64 (x86_64).
                ----------
                Requires: CorePure64 (64-bit userspace). Will not run
                on 32-bit Core or Core64 mixed userspace.
                ----------
                Load:
                $ tce-load -i docker.tcz
                ----------
                Start daemon:
                $ sudo /usr/local/etc/init.d/docker start
                ----------
                Stock TC 17.x: overlay.ko in core modules; no custom kernel
                needed for hello-world. Init uses cgroup v1 (no CGROUP_BPF)
                and iptables:false (no legacy iptables NAT tables).
                .dep pulls net-bridging-KERNEL, ipv6-netfilter-KERNEL,
                nftables (+ libs), iptables, bridge-utils, openssl,
                ca-certificates.
                ----------
                Networking note (stock TC 17, no kernel rebuild):
                TC disables iptables-legacy NAT tables, so default
                daemon.json sets "iptables": false. Enough for
                hello-world; containers do not get outbound NAT.
                Workarounds without changing the kernel:
                1) Host network (simplest):
                   $ docker run --rm --network host IMAGE
                2) Manual nft MASQUERADE/forward for docker0 after
                   dockerd starts (needs nftables + ipv6-netfilter
                   modules). Can be added to init.d/bootsync.
                3) iptables-nft userspace (if provided) so Docker's
                   iptables calls hit nf_tables via nft_compat.
                4) Host HTTP(S)_PROXY for pulls/APIs only.
                Custom kernel only needed later for full legacy
                iptables NAT or cgroup v2 + CONFIG_CGROUP_BPF.
                ----------
                Persist across boots (Tiny Core filetool):
                Add these paths to /opt/.filetool.lst (no leading /):
                etc/passwd
                etc/group
                etc/shadow
                etc/gshadow
                etc/docker
                opt/bootsync.sh
                Then run: filetool.sh -b
                Notes:
                - etc/passwd + etc/group (+ shadow/gshadow) keep the
                  docker group and tc membership created at load time.
                - etc/docker keeps daemon.json and any certs/config
                  under /etc/docker.
                - opt/bootsync.sh if you auto-start dockerd on boot
                  (see below). Also backup opt/.filetool.lst itself
                  via normal TC mydata habit.
                Do NOT put var/lib/docker in .filetool.lst (images and
                volumes are large). Bind-mount or use a dedicated
                partition for /var/lib/docker instead, e.g. in
                bootsync: mkdir -p /mnt/sda1/docker-data &&
                mount --bind /mnt/sda1/docker-data /var/lib/docker
                (adjust device/path). Without that, images/containers
                are lost on reboot.
                ----------
                Optional bootsync (/opt/bootsync.sh):
                /usr/local/etc/init.d/docker start
                ----------
                This extension contains:
                docker-29.10.0 static - Apache-2.0 -
                https://download.docker.com/linux/static/stable/x86_64/
                ----------
